<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-14828] No fallback to full rebalance after exception on historical</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-14828</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;We have noticed that in some cases when we handle demand message in &lt;tt&gt;GridDhtPartitionSupplier.java&lt;/tt&gt; it is possible for some reasons that&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
iter = grp.offheap().rebalanceIterator(demandMsg.partitions(), demandMsg.topologyVersion());
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;throw an exception. In that case, rebalance should switch to full, but the code has a bug and &lt;tt&gt;remainingParts&lt;/tt&gt; has been filed after rebalance iterator has been created&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
                &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; i = 0; i &amp;lt; histMap.size(); i++) {
                    &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; p = histMap.partitionAt(i);

                    remainingParts.add(p);
                }
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That means that we lost partitions that meant to be rebalanced by historical rebalance.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The solution is to create an iterator after &lt;tt&gt;remainingParts&lt;/tt&gt; filling.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
